Programmatic API

 Light Air provides programmatic API with
 the {{{../apidocs/net/sf/lightair/LightAirApi.html}net.sf.lightair.LightAirApi class}}.

 The general contract is to {{{../apidocs/net/sf/lightair/LightAirApi.html#initialize-java.lang.String-}initialize}}
 and {{{../apidocs/net/sf/lightair/LightAirApi.html#shutdown--}shutdown}}
 and in between perform either {{{../apidocs/net/sf/lightair/LightAirApi.html#generateXsd--}generateXsd}} call
 or (a series of) {{{../apidocs/net/sf/lightair/LightAirApi.html#setup-java.util.Map-}setup}}
 and {{{../apidocs/net/sf/lightair/LightAirApi.html#verify-java.util.Map-}verify}}
 or {{{../apidocs/net/sf/lightair/LightAirApi.html#await-java.util.Map-}await}} calls.

 To generate XSD files:

+---+
LightAirApi.initialize(LightAirApi.getPropertiesFileName());
LightAirApi.generateXsd();
LightAirApi.shutdown();
+---+

 To setup and verify database:

+---+
Map<String, List<String>> fileNames = new HashMap<>();
fileNames.put(Keywords.DEFAULT_PROFILE, Arrays.asList("my-dataset-1.xml", "my-dataset-2.xml"));

LightAirApi.initialize(LightAirApi.getPropertiesFileName());
LightAirApi.setup(fileNames);
// ...execute function under test...
LightAirApi.verify(fileNames);
// ...or for asynchronous functionality:
LightAirApi.await(fileNames);
// ...possibly repeat setup and verify / await for other tests...
LightAirApi.shutdown();
+---+

